(3122473, 437393, 53814, '<td valign="top">One of the more creative compositions in this challenge. I would score this higher if the lighting on the skateboarder was more consistant with the overall lighting (less intense and coming from the upper left) My monitor (on a Mac browser) is also showing some loss of detail in the block wall. Keep that creativity coming - 7</td>', 'One of the more creative compositions in this challenge. I would score this higher if the lighting on the skateboarder was more consistant with the overall lighting (less intense and coming from the upper left) My monitor (on a Mac browser) is also showing some loss of detail in the block wall. Keep that creativity coming - 7', '2006-12-15 22:21:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3122475, 438634, 66384, '<td valign="top">Lovely.</td>', 'Lovely.', '2006-12-15 22:21:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3122477, 437571, 67841, '<td valign="top">Borderline DNMC, IMO - but a beautiful shot nonetheless :: I''m gonna guess your counting on all that sky reflecting the water to count, right?  :: Seems you left a fair bit of sensor dust despite having rules wide open to anything ::  A really great moment, but it would have met the challenge more if you had framed the pier along the bottom &amp; gave us a whole lotta sky - no one could have faulted you for missing the assignment then.<br/> <br/>&lt;&lt; 6 &gt;&gt;</td>', 'Borderline DNMC, IMO - but a beautiful shot nonetheless :: I''m gonna guess your counting on all that sky reflecting the water to count, right?  :: Seems you left a fair bit of sensor dust despite having rules wide open to anything ::  A really great moment, but it would have met the challenge more if you had framed the pier along the bottom & gave us a whole lotta sky - no one could have faulted you for missing the assignment then. << 6 >>', '2006-12-15 22:21:58.000000', NULL, 1),
