(3122617, 438663, 53814, '<td valign="top">The concept is excellent, the selection/extract technique on the hands needs help. If you photograph the fingers on a white background and then extract them and paste into the shot you will have real looking hands and complete control over their exposure. Also, if a challenge offers you 720 pixels to work with, you should use all of them to increase your score. To me, the concept alone is worth a 7.</td>', 'The concept is excellent, the selection/extract technique on the hands needs help. If you photograph the fingers on a white background and then extract them and paste into the shot you will have real looking hands and complete control over their exposure. Also, if a challenge offers you 720 pixels to work with, you should use all of them to increase your score. To me, the concept alone is worth a 7.', '2006-12-15 23:49:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(3122628, 438768, 17203, '<td valign="top">Hmm... a challenge custom-made for Larus, but just in case there''s ANY doubt, let''s schedule it at the same time as an X3-class solar flare so there will be photographic nirvana sitting right outside his window. I think with a wider angle, you''d find that the streams of light spell out your name. <i>Oh, and just for kicks, let''s have heavy fog over at Shannon''s house at the same time while he''s setting up the telescope.</i> Curse you, foul ribbon hog of the far north!<br/> <br/>At least you had the dignity to keep the size below 720 pixels so the shot we vote on after this doesn''t get an automatic 1 by comparison. Yeah, it''s another 10, but this is the last one you get dammit! I''m burning my mouse after I click the button, I swear. ;-P</td>', 'Hmm... a challenge custom-made for Larus, but just in case there''s ANY doubt, let''s schedule it at the same time as an X3-class solar flare so there will be photographic nirvana sitting right outside his window. I think with a wider angle, you''d find that the streams of light spell out your name. Oh, and just for kicks, let''s have heavy fog over at Shannon''s house at the same time while he''s setting up the telescope. Curse you, foul ribbon hog of the far north! At least you had the dignity to keep the size below 720 pixels so the shot we vote on after this doesn''t get an automatic 1 by comparison. Yeah, it''s another 10, but this is the last one you get dammit! I''m burning my mouse after I click the button, I swear. ;-P', '2006-12-15 23:58:09.000000', NULL, 1),
