(3136253, 438849, 66201, '<td valign="top">You sent mail asking me: Pleas let me know, why do you thought that my photo-entry for Sky, titled "Sky High Fish Eye Lens", did not meet the challenge? I know it did need some technical improvements. I learned it is hard to photograph a fish, closeup, from the side, in an aquarium. They just keep turning to see you.<br/> <br/>Recently, the **First place winner** for "Dirt" had mostly, pictures of cows.<br/>It could have been shot at a lower angle with More of the dirt showing to Emphasis Dirt, which was the challenge. That seemed an excellent entry for an "Animal" or "Cow" Challenge. Yet it came in 1st place.<br/> <br/> <br/>DNMC: "Make the sky a key element of your photograph". When the image is first uploaded, I see an out of focus fish. Because this is a "Sky" challeneg, I sit and wonder what a fish ahs to do with the challenge....then I see the refelection in the fish''s eye and realise what you were going for. The sky is  not a "key element of your photograph"...but just my opinion.</td>', 'You sent mail asking me: Pleas let me know, why do you thought that my photo-entry for Sky, titled "Sky High Fish Eye Lens", did not meet the challenge? I know it did need some technical improvements. I learned it is hard to photograph a fish, closeup, from the side, in an aquarium. They just keep turning to see you. Recently, the **First place winner** for "Dirt" had mostly, pictures of cows.It could have been shot at a lower angle with More of the dirt showing to Emphasis Dirt, which was the challenge. That seemed an excellent entry for an "Animal" or "Cow" Challenge. Yet it came in 1st place.  DNMC: "Make the sky a key element of your photograph". When the image is first uploaded, I see an out of focus fish. Because this is a "Sky" challeneg, I sit and wonder what a fish ahs to do with the challenge....then I see the refelection in the fish''s eye and realise what you were going for. The sky is  not a "key element of your photograph"...but just my opinion.', '2006-12-20 15:30:42.000000', NULL, 1),
