(3143648, 438552, 40683, '<td valign="top">Just beautiful...A wonderful balance of drama and serenity, simultaneously stimulating and soothing to the senses.</td>', 'Just beautiful...A wonderful balance of drama and serenity, simultaneously stimulating and soothing to the senses.', '2006-12-22 23:21:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3143661, 437270, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by slickchik:</b></div><hr/><i> I am jealous that this is only minutes away from your house.  For me to get something like this I have to drive at least 45-60 minutes.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>More like 5 minutes; less if there''s no traffic, like at dawn... I am lucky :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by slickchik: I am jealous that this is only minutes away from your house.  For me to get something like this I have to drive at least 45-60 minutes.  More like 5 minutes; less if there''s no traffic, like at dawn... I am lucky :-)', '2006-12-22 23:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3143677, 436806, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> 7 for the mostly invisible giant beer-bottle who is apparently eating Miami. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Oh, you had it completely right until you got to Miami -- that''s a <b>pine</b> -- not a <b>palm</b> tree there ... : )</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: 7 for the mostly invisible giant beer-bottle who is apparently eating Miami.  Oh, you had it completely right until you got to Miami -- that''s a pine -- not a palm tree there ... : )', '2006-12-22 23:47:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3143721, 438571, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very nice Gary!  I''d love to hear a bit about the postprocessing... care to share?  (I''m mainly interested in what you did in processing Tara, I love the look you are getting on your model''s shots.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-23 00:16:10.</i></td>', 'Very nice Gary!  I''d love to hear a bit about the postprocessing... care to share?  (I''m mainly interested in what you did in processing Tara, I love the look you are getting on your model''s shots.)', '2006-12-23 00:14:03.000000', '2006-12-23 00:16:10.000000', 0),
(3143850, 438571, 5728, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments and votes. This first "expert" editing challenge was fun. I will miss out the next few though until things settle down and some issues are sorted out.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nshapiro:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nice Gary!  I''d love to hear a bit about the postprocessing... care to share?  (I''m mainly interested in what you did in processing Tara, I love the look you are getting on your model''s shots.) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>To tell you the truth I can''t remember exactly what I did. I can tell you though that I am keeping more and more away from filters now than in the past and using mainly on Photoshop tools like curves, levels, selective color etc and a lot of masking.</td>', 'Thanks for all your comments and votes. This first "expert" editing challenge was fun. I will miss out the next few though until things settle down and some issues are sorted out. Originally posted by nshapiro: Very nice Gary!  I''d love to hear a bit about the postprocessing... care to share?  (I''m mainly interested in what you did in processing Tara, I love the look you are getting on your model''s shots.)   To tell you the truth I can''t remember exactly what I did. I can tell you though that I am keeping more and more away from filters now than in the past and using mainly on Photoshop tools like curves, levels, selective color etc and a lot of masking.', '2006-12-23 02:11:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3143891, 438768, 70320, '<td valign="top">This is really fentastic work keep it up!</td>', 'This is really fentastic work keep it up!', '2006-12-23 03:23:54.000000', NULL, 0),
